---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"
import { faqs } from "../../data/docs-content"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="troubleshooting">

          <p>
            Fixes for common problems, answers to frequent questions, and how to delete your Vector account.
          </p>

          <h2 id="common-problems">Common problems</h2>
          <div class="troubleshooting">
            <article><strong>The agent does not respond</strong><p>Confirm a provider and model are connected, then check whether the provider reports a quota or authentication error.</p></article>
            <article><strong>The browser cannot open the app</strong><p>Start the development server in Terminal and use the local URL printed by the project.</p></article>
            <article><strong>A workspace cannot be created</strong><p>Open a repository first and confirm the folder is writable. Git repositories provide the cleanest isolated-workspace flow.</p></article>
            <article><strong>A deployment fails</strong><p>Open the deployment log, verify the build command and output directory, and check required environment values.</p></article>
            <article><strong>macOS says Vector cannot be opened</strong><p>Preview builds are not yet notarized by Apple, so macOS blocks them on first launch. Try to open Vector once, then go to System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security, find the message about Vector, and choose Open Anyway. Or run <code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Vector.app</code> in Terminal. You only need to do this once.</p></article>
            <article><strong>Windows shows a SmartScreen warning</strong><p>Preview installers are not yet code-signed. Choose More info, then Run anyway.</p></article>
            <article><strong>The Linux AppImage does not start</strong><p>Make the file executable first with <code>chmod +x</code> on the downloaded AppImage, then run it.</p></article>
            <article><strong>Vector 1.99.99 does not open on an Intel Mac, Windows on Arm or Linux on Arm</strong><p>Those 1.99.99 builds are missing the terminal component for their processor, and a copy that does not open never checks for updates. Download 1.99.100 or later from your account page, or from <a href="https://github.com/scr1pter/Vectordev.ai/releases/latest">GitHub releases</a> without an account, and install it over the old one; your projects and settings stay where they are.</p></article>
            <article><strong>Vector never offers an update</strong><p>Open Settings → Updates &amp; about and choose Check now, or choose Check for Updates in the Vector menu on macOS. When the update has downloaded, choose Restart to update (Restart in the macOS menu's dialog). Versions before 1.99.2 have no Updates &amp; about page: choose Update Vector at the bottom of the left sidebar, which downloads the update and restarts in one step. On Linux, in-app updates only work when you run the AppImage itself. If no update appears, download the latest version from your account page, or from <a href="https://github.com/scr1pter/Vectordev.ai/releases/latest">GitHub releases</a> without an account, and install it over the old one; your projects and settings stay where they are.</p></article>
            <article><strong>A macOS update does not install</strong><p>If Restart to update (Restart in the Vector menu's update dialog, or Update Vector before 1.99.2) does nothing or shows an error, or Vector closes and does not reopen, first quit Vector if it is still open. Then download the DMG from your account page or <a href="https://github.com/scr1pter/Vectordev.ai/releases/latest">GitHub releases</a>, drag Vector to Applications to replace the old copy, and open it from Applications. Your projects and settings stay where they are.</p></article>
          </div>

          <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <div class="faq-list">
            {faqs.map((item) => (
              <details>
                <summary><span>{item.question}</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
                <p>{item.answer}</p>
              </details>
            ))}
          </div>

          <h2 id="delete-account">Delete your account</h2>
          <p>
            You can delete your Vector account yourself, from the account page. It cannot be undone, so Vector asks you
            to type your own email address first.
          </p>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li><span /><div><strong>Open your account</strong><p>Go to <a href="/account">vectordev.ai/account</a> and sign in.</p></div></li>
            <li><span /><div><strong>Scroll to Account</strong><p>The last section on the page, under Sign out, has <strong>Delete account…</strong>.</p></div></li>
            <li><span /><div><strong>Type your email to confirm</strong><p>The delete button stays disabled until the address you type matches the one on the account.</p></div></li>
          </ol>

          <h3 id="what-deletion-does">What deletion does</h3>
          <dl class="doc-rows">
            <div><dt>Your sign-in</dt><dd>The account and its email and name are deleted. You can create a new account with the same address afterwards; it will not be the same account, and nothing is restored to it.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>CLI tokens</dt><dd>Revoked, so a terminal already signed in with <code>vector login</code> stops verifying. Without this they would keep working until they expired, up to ninety days later.</dd></div>
          </dl>

          <h3 id="what-deletion-does-not-touch">What deletion does not touch</h3>
          <p>
            Your repositories, your sessions and Vector's memory live on your own machine, and deleting the account does
            not reach them. Remove them yourself: sessions and memory are in Vector's data directory (<code>vector db
            path</code> prints where the database is), and <code>vector uninstall</code> removes the CLI and its files.
            Anything you published to your own Vercel, Netlify or Supabase account belongs to those accounts and stays
            there.
          </p>

          <p class="note">
            If the account page reports that deletion is not configured, nothing was changed. Write to support and it
            will be done by hand.
          </p>
</DocsPage>
